Post — authors and attribution
=============================

Post is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later. See COPYING for the full text.

Post is a fork of Stamp, and a large part of what you are running was
written by other people. This file records who.


Post
----

Post's own work — the profiles system, the calendar integration and the
mail/calendar bridge, the contact editor and photo cropper, the mail
layouts and sidebar agenda, the badge system, the Flatpak and native
packaging, and the rebranding — is:

    Copyright 2026 steeb-k <skaznak@protonmail.com>

Post was forked from Stamp at commit 61a1da4 on 2026-08-05.
Files created for Post carry only the copyright above. Files inherited
from Stamp keep their original notices; where Post has substantially
rewritten one, a second notice is added below the original rather than
replacing it.


Stamp (upstream)
----------------

Post is a fork of Stamp:

    https://gitlab.gnome.org/jbrummer/stamp

Roughly two thirds of Post outside the vendored calendar is Stamp's code.
The mail backend, the message and conversation lists, the composer, the
MIME parser, the account and session handling, the web view, the contact
list, PGP and S/MIME support, BIMI and one-click unsubscribe are all
Stamp's work, as is the application's overall shape.

    Jan-Michael Brummer <jan.brummer@tabos.org>   — author and maintainer
    Michael Catanzaro <mcatanzaro@gnome.org>
    Adrien Plazas <aplazas@gnome.org>
    Giacomo Leidi <therewasa@fishinthecalculator.me>
    Tobias Bernard <tbernard@gnome.org>           — design
    Chris Pouliot <chrispouliot@icloud.com>

Post is not affiliated with Stamp and is not endorsed by its authors.
Bugs in Post should be reported to Post, not to Stamp.


GNOME Calendar (vendored)
-------------------------

src/gcal/ is a vendored copy of GNOME Calendar, built into Post as a
static library to provide the calendar views, event editor and calendar
management:

    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-calendar

Every file there keeps its upstream copyright and license notice
unchanged. Post's changes to that tree are small and are kept in separate
commits so they can be re-applied to a newer snapshot; see
src/gcal/VENDORED.md for the vendored commit and the list of local
changes.

Copyright holders in the vendored tree include:

    Georges Basile Stavracas Neto <georges.stavracas@gmail.com>
    Erick Pérez Castellanos <erickpc@gnome.org>
    Alen Galinec <mind.on.warp@gmail.com>
    Titouan Real <titouan.real@gmail.com>
    Diego Iván M.E <diegoivan.mae@gmail.com>
    Markus Göllnitz <camelcasenick@bewares.it>
    Federico Mena Quintero <federico@gnome.org>
    Florian Brosch <flo.brosch@gmail.com>
    Vamsi Krishna Gollapudi <pandu.sonu@yahoo.com>
    Yash Singh <yashdev10p@gmail.com>
    Benjamin Otte
    Purism SPC
    Red Hat, Inc.

together with the GTK authors, for the small pieces of GTK carried in
src/gcal/contrib/.


